WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.085
Many notes still call the

2
00:00:02.085 --> 00:00:03.994
reverse repo the floor for

3
00:00:03.994 --> 00:00:05.242
short-term rates.

4
00:00:05.496 --> 00:00:07.601
Since 2022, it isn't.

5
00:00:07.865 --> 00:00:09.453
The RBI steers overnight

6
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:10.842
rates with a corridor

7
00:00:10.957 --> 00:00:13.058
around its policy repo rate.

8
00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:14.791
The ceiling is the Marginal

9
00:00:14.791 --> 00:00:15.985
Standing Facility rate,

10
00:00:16.532 --> 00:00:17.989
a quarter point above repo.

11
00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:21.581
In April 2022, a new floor arrived:

12
00:00:22.174 --> 00:00:24.098
the Standing Deposit Facility,

13
00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:26.125
a quarter point below, with

14
00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.409
no collateral needed.

15
00:00:27.985 --> 00:00:29.750
The fixed-rate reverse repo

16
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.188
stayed in the toolkit,

17
00:00:31.549 --> 00:00:32.843
but outside the corridor.

18
00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:35.101
As of October 2026:

19
00:00:35.431 --> 00:00:36.960
repo 5.5,

20
00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:39.733
deposit facility 5.25,

21
00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:42.538
MSF 5.75 percent.

22
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:43.984
Learn the corridor,

23
00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:45.237
not just the rate.

24
00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:46.282
Your turn.

25
00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:48.137
Which facility is now the

26
00:00:48.137 --> 00:00:49.879
floor of the RBI's corridor?
